{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwdmVq5zh1Ecnz7T9f89","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. The rule has already run once with status `ok`, so its query works against the index. I haven't opened the dashboard to check that each panel shows data.\n\n**1. What the data holds.** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` data view (time field `timestamp`) is one record per web request. Each record has:\n- **Request details:** `request`, `url`, `extension`, `agent`, `referer`\n- **Response details:** the HTTP code in `response` (stored as text, with an exact-match version `response.keyword`) and size in `bytes`\n- **Visitor details:** client IP in `clientip`, location in `geo.src` / `geo.dest` / `geo.coordinates`, operating system in `machine.os`, plus `host` and `tags`\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-1a5856bf Web logs overview\"** (7 panels): http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-1a5856bf-web-logs-overview-8220daa1faff\n- Three single-number panels: total requests, unique visitors (distinct client IPs) and total bytes served\n- Requests over time, split by the top 5 response codes\n- A pie chart of the share of each response code\n- A table of the top 10 URLs, with request count and average bytes\n- Requests by the top 10 source countries\n\n**3. Alert rule \"EFF-1a5856bf 5xx spike\"** (id `e68ed653-03ad-42dc-beff-7e1be8eafc97`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`. Every minute it counts requests from the last 5 minutes with a response code from 500 to 599, and fires when the count is more than 10. Because the codes are stored as text, this works as a text comparison, which is correct here since they're all three-digit numbers. It has no notification action attached, so when it fires it shows up in Kibana but doesn't send anything anywhere."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":228,"cache_read_input_tokens":20430,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":228},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"334eabbb-fc7a-420e-93c0-cbb7f0373518","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:29:44.191Z","request_id":"req_011CfwdmVcCoGibMoVrV3rvc"}
